(4595348, 661502, 48471, '<td valign="top">This made me laugh... While looking at this photo, I have to take a position, a role, and considering the challenge, I think of myself as the police man. Well, the only place I''ve seen the mugshot genre is at the smoking gun, so... Now, I feel bad for arresting this guy.<br/>A very smart and lighthearted presentation.</td>', 'This made me laugh... While looking at this photo, I have to take a position, a role, and considering the challenge, I think of myself as the police man. Well, the only place I''ve seen the mugshot genre is at the smoking gun, so... Now, I feel bad for arresting this guy.A very smart and lighthearted presentation.', '2008-03-29 11:30:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595600, 661222, 48471, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the title; at first, I got scared from the photo, it''s done very well, with piercing eyes and a strong shadow. But then, I read the title and loled.</td>', 'Thanks for the title; at first, I got scared from the photo, it''s done very well, with piercing eyes and a strong shadow. But then, I read the title and loled.', '2008-03-29 13:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595640, 660727, 88352, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites here.  Very nice job.</td>', 'One of my favorites here.  Very nice job.', '2008-03-29 14:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595641, 661461, 88352, '<td valign="top">I like the hint of a sports jersey.</td>', 'I like the hint of a sports jersey.', '2008-03-29 14:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595668, 660808, 17986, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a great shot! You really captured the feeling of nothingness one feels while being incarcerated. Great interpretation! 10 ;-]</td>', 'Wow, what a great shot! You really captured the feeling of nothingness one feels while being incarcerated. Great interpretation! 10 ;-]', '2008-03-29 15:11:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595669, 660738, 17986, '<td valign="top">The light looks pretty harsh in this one. Some diffused side light would have softened up the shadows and given it more depth. The composition is off a little too IMO. I wouldn''t have gone for a center weighted comp here, but if you do want it centered, be sure that you are not cutting of anything that is thematic to the shot. Peace is sort of the theme here, yet the peace gestures are cut off.<br/> <br/>The focus and DOF look pretty good here. The colors and exposure are well done. Nothing is blown out.</td>', 'The light looks pretty harsh in this one. Some diffused side light would have softened up the shadows and given it more depth. The composition is off a little too IMO. I wouldn''t have gone for a center weighted comp here, but if you do want it centered, be sure that you are not cutting of anything that is thematic to the shot. Peace is sort of the theme here, yet the peace gestures are cut off. The focus and DOF look pretty good here. The colors and exposure are well done. Nothing is blown out.', '2008-03-29 15:17:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595672, 661437, 17986, '<td valign="top">I''ve got to be honest here, I don''t think this really meets the challenge. That being said, it is still a really nice pic. I kinda wish the background contrasted more with the subject, but I realize it''s hard to get a duck to stand where you want it and pose.</td>', 'I''ve got to be honest here, I don''t think this really meets the challenge. That being said, it is still a really nice pic. I kinda wish the background contrasted more with the subject, but I realize it''s hard to get a duck to stand where you want it and pose.', '2008-03-29 15:21:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595681, 660647, 17986, '<td valign="top">I like portraits of old people. There is always so much character in their faces. I like the expression here, nice pose.<br/> <br/>Here are a couple of things I would suggest:<br/> <br/>      Use some side lighting to add depth. If you don''t have lights, use a window. Then use your shutter speed to control the strength of the available light.<br/>      Have your subject stand farther from the background  and select a larger aperture. This will create a more narrow depth of field and "blur out" distracting background elements like wrinkles/folds in your backdrop.</td>', 'I like portraits of old people. There is always so much character in their faces. I like the expression here, nice pose. Here are a couple of things I would suggest:       Use some side lighting to add depth. If you don''t have lights, use a window. Then use your shutter speed to control the strength of the available light.      Have your subject stand farther from the background  and select a larger aperture. This will create a more narrow depth of field and "blur out" distracting background elements like wrinkles/folds in your backdrop.', '2008-03-29 15:29:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595682, 659138, 17986, '<td valign="top">This looks like a nice capture, but it''s a little over-processed for my taste.</td>', 'This looks like a nice capture, but it''s a little over-processed for my taste.', '2008-03-29 15:30:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595868, 660037, 48479, '<td valign="top">classic</td>', 'classic', '2008-03-29 18:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595892, 660528, 29011, '<td valign="top">I had no idea Anne Sparkz was married to the toothfairy LOL. I''m split between yours and Timfy''s shot. They both have the humor we love seeing from you and good technicals. Your expression and expressive eyes are way funny, in a good way of course. What may inch Timfy''s shot ahead is the classic mug shot look of the white background and lighting but since I saw the toothfairy character before it doesn''t have that first view wow but still very funny. So I rate your two shots equally. I expect to at least see this in the top10 or even ribbon. Good luck.</td>', 'I had no idea Anne Sparkz was married to the toothfairy LOL. I''m split between yours and Timfy''s shot. They both have the humor we love seeing from you and good technicals. Your expression and expressive eyes are way funny, in a good way of course. What may inch Timfy''s shot ahead is the classic mug shot look of the white background and lighting but since I saw the toothfairy character before it doesn''t have that first view wow but still very funny. So I rate your two shots equally. I expect to at least see this in the top10 or even ribbon. Good luck.', '2008-03-29 18:47:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595898, 660037, 29011, '<td valign="top">Too funny! LOL. The classic mug shot look alright. Would be really authentic if you had those height markings in the background. Fun to seee the Tooth Fairy again. A series of these would be too funny. Always fun to see you and Aimee duke it out in the challenges. I''m rooting for both of your shots to make the top10. Maybe make the front page even. Good luck!</td>', 'Too funny! LOL. The classic mug shot look alright. Would be really authentic if you had those height markings in the background. Fun to seee the Tooth Fairy again. A series of these would be too funny. Always fun to see you and Aimee duke it out in the challenges. I''m rooting for both of your shots to make the top10. Maybe make the front page even. Good luck!', '2008-03-29 18:52:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4595906, 661444, 29011, '<td valign="top">Cool idea. You cleaned up nicely ;) With the non cluttered simple layout it looks more like before and after. For a master of disguise layout I imagine you sitting at a desk with spy related things on the desk. A magnifying glass, top secret folder,etc.. A top5 fave.</td>', 'Cool idea. You cleaned up nicely ;) With the non cluttered simple layout it looks more like before and after. For a master of disguise layout I imagine you sitting at a desk with spy related things on the desk. A magnifying glass, top secret folder,etc.. A top5 fave.', '2008-03-29 19:03:13.000000', NULL, 1),
